data.content:
Three breaking changes hit your code in EF Core 10. Here's each one and the fix:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — now takes `Func`, not `Expression<Func>`

Your expression tree code **won't compile**. Replace it with a simple lambda:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more manual `Expression.Call` / `Expression.Lambda` needed.

---

### 2. Complex type columns — now auto-uniquified & nested paths changed

**Same-level:** `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street` previously shared one column silently. EF 10 appends a number (e.g. `Street`, `Street1`). If you have an existing DB and want to keep shared columns, pin them explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});
```

**Nested:** `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` was mapped to column `BillingAddress_City`. Now it's `Payment_BillingAddress_City` (full path). To preserve the old name:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

> ⚠️ If you don't fix these, EF will generate a migration that renames/adds columns, breaking your existing schema.

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method gained a `string logCommandText` parameter (for redacted SQL logging). Add it:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // <-- new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (sensitive data redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual SQL
    }
}
```

Update **all** methods on the interface (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) similarly.
